00:50:55.820 --> 00:50:57.660
It also goes very quickly.
而且进行得非常快。

1031
00:50:57.660 --> 00:50:59.600
In about three sentences, W.B.
大约三句话，W.B.

1032
00:50:59.700 --> 00:51:03.260
Jones agrees, fine, you can have your parking spaces back.
琼斯就同意了，好吧，你们可以拿回你们的停车位了。

1033
00:51:03.360 --> 00:51:03.980
It's a triumph.
这是一次胜利。

1034
00:51:04.280 --> 00:51:08.760
Listen, it looks like Kevin's about to cry and Bill Kress is not here for that.
听着，凯文看起来快要哭了，而比尔·克雷斯可不想看到那个。

1035
00:51:08.960 --> 00:51:12.020
He can't handle a grown man crying about a parking spot.
他受不了一个大男人为了一个停车位哭泣。

1036
00:51:12.180 --> 00:51:13.780
And so Paul Faust calls it.
所以保罗·福斯特做了决定。

1037
00:51:13.900 --> 00:51:15.420
He's like, just give them their spots back.
他说，就把车位还给他们吧。

1038
00:51:15.420 --> 00:51:17.280
And it just wraps up so quickly.
事情就这样很快结束了。

1039
00:51:17.620 --> 00:51:18.120
It does.
确实。

1040
00:51:18.300 --> 00:51:21.080
And then Paul has a great line where he says this could have been an email.
然后保罗有一句很棒的台词，他说这本来可以发封邮件解决的。

1041
00:51:21.400 --> 00:51:22.580
Which is like a meme.
这就像一个梗。

1042
00:51:22.780 --> 00:51:24.080
It also speaks to me.
这也说到了我的心坎里。

1043
00:51:24.520 --> 00:51:24.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1044
00:51:25.100 --> 00:51:28.580
I mean, Paul needs to get out and ride his motorcycle.
我是说，保罗需要出去骑他的摩托车了。

1045
00:51:29.140 --> 00:51:29.840
He's done.
他受够了。

1046
00:51:31.200 --> 00:51:34.360
Kevin's talking head after this scene broke my heart.
这场戏之后凯文的采访片段让我心碎。

1047
00:51:34.840 --> 00:51:36.580
Brian did such a good job with it.
布莱恩演得太棒了。

1048
00:51:36.800 --> 00:51:41.280
He just says that after Stacey broke up with him, it was really a tough time.
他只是说在史黛西和他分手后，那真是一段艰难的时光。

1049
00:51:41.520 --> 00:51:44.500
And well, it's just nice to win one.
嗯，能赢一次真好。

1050
00:51:44.780 --> 00:51:46.060
And he tears up.
然后他流泪了。

1051
00:51:46.220 --> 00:51:47.560
It was so sweet.
那真是太贴心了。

1052
00:51:47.560 --> 00:51:55.220
Guys, we didn't go to the character of Kevin very often for a heartfelt moment on the show.
伙计们，在剧中我们很少让凯文这个角色展现深情时刻。

1053
00:51:55.400 --> 00:52:00.980
And it's a shame because Brian Baumgartner is a fantastic actor.
这挺可惜的，因为布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳是一位出色的演员。

1054
00:52:01.240 --> 00:52:01.480
Yeah.
没错。

1055
00:52:01.480 --> 00:52:04.040
And you can see that in this talking head.
你们可以在这段采访中看出来。

1056
00:52:04.400 --> 00:52:04.880
Yeah.
没错。

1057
00:52:05.020 --> 00:52:08.340
I was excited to get to see this performance from him.
我很高兴能看到他这段表演。

1058
00:52:08.800 --> 00:52:09.620
Great job, Bea.
干得好，比。

1059
00:52:10.280 --> 00:52:10.700
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1060
00:52:10.800 --> 00:52:13.840
Michael has come back from his date and he's very angry.
迈克尔约会回来了，他非常生气。

1061
00:52:14.260 --> 00:52:14.800
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1062
00:52:15.000 --> 00:52:16.660
He gives a big speech.
他发表了一大通演说。

1063
00:52:17.200 --> 00:52:19.880
Angela, here are the things that he's a man of.
安吉拉，以下是他所具备的品质。

1064
00:52:20.560 --> 00:52:21.080
Intensity.
激情。

1065
00:52:21.320 --> 00:52:21.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1066
00:52:22.000 --> 00:52:22.420
Cool.
酷。

1067
00:52:22.940 --> 00:52:23.420
Youth.
年轻。

1068
00:52:23.640 --> 00:52:24.660
And passionately.
还有热情。

1069
00:52:25.400 --> 00:52:26.980
He's a man of passionately.
他是个有热情的人。

1070
00:52:26.980 --> 00:52:30.100
He's a man of youth and passionately.
他是个有年轻和热情的人。

1071
00:52:31.600 --> 00:52:36.800
Well, at 15 minutes, 10 seconds, you might notice I'm writing on the top of my desk.
嗯，在15分10秒的时候，你们可能会注意到我在桌面上写字。

1072
00:52:36.940 --> 00:52:41.940
I have several papers on this very little thin lip of the top of my desk.
我的办公桌边缘非常窄，上面放了几张纸。

1073
00:52:42.480 --> 00:52:48.740
I had to do that for camera because when I was staging my writing on the actual desk,
我不得不为了拍摄这么做，因为如果我在桌面上正常写字的话，

1074
00:52:48.900 --> 00:52:51.000
they couldn't see my face when Michael entered.
迈克尔进来时他们就拍不到我的脸了。

1075
00:52:51.280 --> 00:52:56.880
I have to imagine that was a tough reach and very awkward because you're leaning over your desk
我能想象那一定很难够到，而且姿势很别扭，因为你得趴在桌子上

1076
00:52:56.980 --> 00:52:59.060
to write on a tiny ledge.
在那个小边缘上写字。

1077
00:52:59.320 --> 00:53:00.800
Well, I'll tell you something.
嗯，我告诉你吧。

1078
00:53:01.020 --> 00:53:04.360
Pam's desk was very narrow in general.
帕姆的桌子整体就很窄。

1079
00:53:04.600 --> 00:53:07.420
I couldn't fit more than a keyboard on it.
除了键盘，我什么都放不下。

1080
00:53:07.600 --> 00:53:13.820
In order to write on Pam's actual desk, which was made very thin, I think, for production,
为了在帕姆真正的桌子上写字——我觉得那桌子为了拍摄做得特别薄——

1081
00:53:14.540 --> 00:53:15.860
it was always awkward.
一直都很别扭。

1082
00:53:16.000 --> 00:53:16.480
Always.
一直都是。

1083
00:53:17.040 --> 00:53:17.380
Yeah.
没错。

1084
00:53:17.580 --> 00:53:20.820
So I've perched up on that little ledge, which was also awkward.
所以我只能在那小边缘上凑合，那也很别扭。

1085
00:53:21.180 --> 00:53:26.140
In this scene, Jenna, it seems like Jim and Pam are just kind of teasing each other.
在这场戏里，珍娜，吉姆和帕姆似乎只是在互相调侃。

1086
00:53:26.140 --> 00:53:28.000
Like, he's like, what were you thinking?
就像他问，你在想什么呢？

1087
00:53:28.240 --> 00:53:29.600
Setting Michael up with your landlord.
竟然把迈克尔介绍给你的房东。

1088
00:53:29.880 --> 00:53:31.160
Now you have to move out.
现在你得搬家了。

1089
00:53:31.380 --> 00:53:32.160
That went horribly.
那场约会糟透了。

1090
00:53:32.660 --> 00:53:33.880
And they're kind of joking.
他们当时是在开玩笑。

1091
00:53:33.980 --> 00:53:36.220
And she's like, maybe I should move in with my boyfriend.
她说，也许我该搬去和男朋友住。

1092
00:53:36.680 --> 00:53:39.100
And then Pam has a moment of vulnerability.
然后帕姆流露出了脆弱的一面。

1093
00:53:39.340 --> 00:53:44.200
And you see it in your face, Jenna, where you're going to be an advocate for yourself.
你可以从你的表情中看出来，珍娜，你开始学会为自己争取了。

1094
00:53:44.400 --> 00:53:45.960
This is something you've been working on.
这是你一直在努力的事情。

1095
00:53:46.440 --> 00:53:47.580
And she says, you know what?
她说，你知道吗？

1096
00:53:47.620 --> 00:53:50.820
I'm only going to move in with my boyfriend if I'm engaged.
除非订婚，否则我才不会搬去和男朋友住。

1097
00:53:51.300 --> 00:53:51.680
Yeah.
没错。

1098
00:53:52.080 --> 00:53:53.600
And Jim doesn't miss a beat.
吉姆反应很快。

1099
00:53:53.600 --> 00:53:54.920
He's like, oh, it's coming.
他说，噢，快了。

1100
00:53:55.220 --> 00:53:56.000
Of course.
当然。

1101
00:53:56.420 --> 00:53:59.940
And then Pam just kind of keeps joking along.
然后帕姆就一直顺着玩笑接话。

1102
00:54:00.100 --> 00:54:01.900
And Jenna, I was like, does Pam?
珍娜，我当时就在想，帕姆知道吗？

1103
00:54:02.080 --> 00:54:05.980
I mean, in the moment, I was positive that Jim was serious.
我是说，在那一刻，我确信吉姆是认真的。

1104
00:54:06.360 --> 00:54:07.520
Does Pam know?
帕姆知道吗？

1105
00:54:07.900 --> 00:54:09.620
Does Pam know he's doing a bit?
帕姆知道他是在演戏吗？

1106
00:54:09.800 --> 00:54:11.860
Does it hit her that he's not?
她意识到他不是在开玩笑了吗？

1107
00:54:11.860 --> 00:54:24.420
I think this maybe, in my backstory, was kind of one of the first times that this idea of them getting engaged or married has really come up.
我想这可能，在我的背景设定里，是他们谈及订婚或结婚这个想法的第一次。

1108
00:54:25.220 --> 00:54:36.660
And that was a reason why I chose to kind of hesitate as well when Pam says, oh, I'm not going to move in with anyone until I'm engaged, is because this idea of being engaged,
这也是为什么当帕姆说“哦，除非订婚，否则我不会和任何人同居”时，我会犹豫的原因，因为订婚这个念头，

1109
00:54:36.660 --> 00:54:41.200
it's not something that I thought they had talked about a lot yet.
我觉得他们还没怎么讨论过。

1110
00:54:41.200 --> 00:54:44.260
No, and that's how it's that's how it reads as an audience.
没错，观众看起来也是这种感觉。

1111
00:54:44.960 --> 00:54:48.740
I loved it because this is how real life stuff comes up.
我很喜欢这一点，因为现实生活中的事就是这样发生的。

1112
00:54:48.880 --> 00:54:52.040
Sometimes it just seeps in to like a mundane conversation.
有时它只是悄悄渗入一段平凡的对话中。

1113
00:54:52.040 --> 00:54:54.160
And then you're like, oh, crap, we're here now.
然后你会想，糟了，我们现在聊到这儿了。

1114
00:54:54.340 --> 00:54:55.680
OK, yes.
好的，没错。

1115
00:54:55.680 --> 00:55:00.160
And so I think Pam isn't totally sure what to do with this conversation.
所以我认为帕姆并不完全确定该如何应对这段对话。

1116
00:55:00.540 --> 00:55:01.400
Was it a bit?
他是在开玩笑吗？

1117
00:55:01.540 --> 00:55:02.460
Is he being serious?
他是认真的吗？

1118
00:55:02.840 --> 00:55:09.000
Now, he has a talking head for the audience where he says, oh, I'm not kidding.
现在，他对着镜头有个独白，他说，哦，我没开玩笑。

1119
00:55:09.460 --> 00:55:12.380
I got this a week after we started dating.
这是我们开始约会一周后我买的。

1120
00:55:12.600 --> 00:55:14.360
And he shows an engagement ring.
然后他展示了一枚订婚戒指。

1121
00:55:15.080 --> 00:55:18.140
And I'm sorry, does he carry it to work with him every day?
抱歉，他是每天都随身带着它去上班吗？

1122
00:55:18.420 --> 00:55:19.420
I don't know.
我不知道。

1123
00:55:19.580 --> 00:55:20.740
Does it live in his pocket?
它是放在他口袋里吗？

1124
00:55:20.960 --> 00:55:23.240
Is he too worried to leave it at his apartment?
他是担心把它留在公寓里不安全吗？

1125
00:55:23.240 --> 00:55:26.360
Like, he has it ready to go.
总之，他随时准备着。

1126
00:55:27.100 --> 00:55:37.420
We had a fan question from Abigail B who said, is the ring Jim shows the camera the ring he proposes with later and the one that Pam wears for the rest of the show?
我们收到一位粉丝Abigail B的提问，她说，吉姆展示给镜头看的那枚戒指，是他后来求婚用的那枚吗？也是帕姆在剧集余下部分一直戴着的那枚吗？

1127
00:55:38.100 --> 00:55:39.760
I think it is.
我想是的。

1128
00:55:40.260 --> 00:55:41.960
I think that it is.
我觉得就是那枚。

1129
00:55:42.060 --> 00:55:47.600
I remember Phil Shea coming up to me and presenting me with a tray of rings.
我记得菲尔·谢伊走过来，向我展示了一托盘的戒指。

1130
00:55:48.040 --> 00:55:54.700
And he and I had a very long conversation about what kind of ring would Jim buy Pam.
我和他进行了一次很长的谈话，讨论吉姆会给帕姆买什么样的戒指。

1131
00:55:55.260 --> 00:55:57.640
Like, Jim's going to hit it out of the park for Pam.
就像是，吉姆一定会为帕姆选到最完美的戒指。

1132
00:55:57.820 --> 00:56:00.980
Remember, Pam was always a little disappointed in her ring from Roy.
记得吗，帕姆一直对罗伊送她的戒指有点失望。

1133
00:56:01.120 --> 00:56:02.120
That was my backstory.
那是我的背景设定。

1134
00:56:02.460 --> 00:56:03.080
The cluster.
那枚碎钻拼成的戒指。

1135
00:56:03.540 --> 00:56:03.920
Yes.
没错。

1136
00:56:03.920 --> 00:56:09.020
And so, Phil was like, what would make Pam's heart sing?
所以，菲尔问我，什么样的戒指会让帕姆心动？

1137
00:56:09.680 --> 00:56:11.620
And I remember picking that ring.
我记得我选了那枚戒指。

1138
00:56:12.460 --> 00:56:14.780
So, yeah, I think it is that ring.
所以，是的，我想就是那枚戒指。

1139
00:56:15.200 --> 00:56:16.660
Pretty bold move, Jim.
真是大胆的举动啊，吉姆。

1140
00:56:17.060 --> 00:56:19.760
Buy it the first week you guys started dating.
你们刚开始约会第一周就买了。

1141
00:56:20.020 --> 00:56:20.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1142
00:56:20.480 --> 00:56:22.660
But I guess he knew he loved her for a long time.
但我猜他早就知道自己爱她很久了。

1143
00:56:23.020 --> 00:56:23.280
Yeah.
没错。

1144
00:56:23.520 --> 00:56:27.340
Well, guys, here's the scene that's in Michael's office that I love.
好了，各位，这是迈克尔办公室里的一场戏，我非常喜欢。

1145
00:56:27.460 --> 00:56:28.700
It's shot a little differently.
它的拍摄手法有点不同。

1146
00:56:28.920 --> 00:56:30.000
This was Jeff Blitz.
这是杰夫·布里茨拍的。

1147
00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:35.940
You know, there's always so many of the same scenes in the same places because we only had
你知道，同样的场景总是在同样的地方拍摄，因为我们只有

1148
00:56:35.940 --> 00:56:36.620
one set.
一个布景。

1149
00:56:36.820 --> 00:56:40.040
And every once in a while, a director would find a fun way to shoot.
偶尔，导演会找到一种有趣的拍摄方式。

1150
00:56:40.300 --> 00:56:44.900
And Jeff Blitz had this idea for this scene between Michael and Dwight that he would just
杰夫·布里茨对迈克尔和德怀特之间的这场戏有个想法，他想直接

1151
00:56:44.900 --> 00:56:53.260
lower the camera a little and shoot at an angle and slowly push in as Dwight convinces Michael
把摄像机放低一点，以一定角度拍摄，并在德怀特说服迈克尔时缓慢推进镜头

1152
00:56:53.260 --> 00:56:55.600
that what he needs is closure.
他需要的是了结。

1153
00:56:55.900 --> 00:56:59.340
And when I watched the scene, there was a brief moment.
当我看到那一幕时，有一个短暂的瞬间。

1154
00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:02.300
That I thought he meant with Jan.
我以为他指的是简。

1155
00:57:02.580 --> 00:57:02.940
Same.
我也是。

1156
00:57:03.100 --> 00:57:04.960
He needs closure with Jan.
他需要和简做个了结。

1157
00:57:05.260 --> 00:57:06.120
But no.
但并不是。

1158
00:57:06.400 --> 00:57:06.700
No.
不是。

1159
00:57:06.840 --> 00:57:08.040
It's with the chair model.
是和那个椅子模特。

1160
00:57:08.480 --> 00:57:10.400
So they head to the cemetery.
于是他们前往墓地。

1161
00:57:10.740 --> 00:57:12.440
Of a woman he's never met.
去见一个他从未谋面的女人。

1162
00:57:12.780 --> 00:57:13.140
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1163
00:57:13.540 --> 00:57:14.360
That's right.
没错。

1164
00:57:14.560 --> 00:57:23.780
And they are going to launch into a tribute to her by singing a version of American Pie.
他们打算通过唱一首改编版的《美国派》来向她致敬。

1165
00:57:24.360 --> 00:57:25.020
Bye.
再见。

1166
00:57:25.260 --> 00:57:27.560
Bye, Miss Chair Model Lady.
再见，椅子模特小姐。

1167
00:57:28.000 --> 00:57:32.210
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1168
00:57:32.210 --> 00:57:36.290
So, you know, the writers actually had a hard time getting a song cleared for this.
所以，你知道，编剧们其实很难为这一段搞定歌曲版权。

1169
00:57:36.870 --> 00:57:37.370
Shocker.
真让人吃惊。

1170
00:57:37.510 --> 00:57:42.950
The first song they were going to parody was Elton John's Candle in the Wind.
他们最初打算恶搞的歌是埃尔顿·约翰的《风中之烛》。

1171
00:57:43.310 --> 00:57:49.050
But they could not get the rights because, here's an interesting bit of trivia, he had
但他们没能拿到版权，因为这里有个有趣的冷知识，他之前

1172
00:57:49.050 --> 00:57:54.270
given permission for the song to be parodied on 30 Rock, and he did not care for the results.
允许过《我为喜剧狂》恶搞这首歌，但他对结果不太满意。

1173
00:57:54.270 --> 00:57:57.630
So he said no more parodies of Candle in the Wind.
所以他说不再允许恶搞《风中之烛》了。

1174
00:57:57.890 --> 00:57:58.210
No.
不会吧。

1175
00:57:58.650 --> 00:57:58.930
Okay.
好吧。

1176
00:57:59.230 --> 00:58:02.950
They also wrote parodies of Legs by ZZ Top.
他们还写了ZZ Top乐队《美腿》的恶搞版。

1177
00:58:03.350 --> 00:58:04.990
She's got legs.
她有一双美腿。

1178
00:58:05.210 --> 00:58:08.010
How is that a song you sing at a gravesite?
怎么会有人在墓地唱这种歌？

1179
00:58:08.190 --> 00:58:11.450
She was a chair model, and you really see her legs in the picture.
她是个椅子模特，而且你在照片里确实能看到她的腿。

1180
00:58:11.830 --> 00:58:13.150
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1181
00:58:13.250 --> 00:58:13.490
Okay.
好吧。

1182
00:58:13.490 --> 00:58:16.990
And then also Ruby Tuesday by the Rolling Stones.
还有滚石乐队的《红宝石星期二》。

1183
00:58:17.350 --> 00:58:19.010
Oh, I love Ruby Tuesday.
噢，我喜欢《红宝石星期二》。

1184
00:58:19.310 --> 00:58:27.250
But the song that got cleared was American Pie, and I'm so glad it did because I really love them in the dark singing.
但最终获批的是《美国派》，我很高兴是这首，因为我真的很喜欢他们在黑暗中唱歌的样子。

1185
00:58:27.970 --> 00:58:32.430
Well, we can't wrap up this episode without this adorable scene.
好吧，如果不提这个可爱的场景，我们就没法结束这一集了。

1186
00:58:32.710 --> 00:58:43.210
Jenna, I literally wrote adorable and highlighted it between Jim and Pam as they're walking to the satellite parking lot, and the sun is setting.
珍娜，我真的写了“可爱”二字，还特意标了出来，就是吉姆和帕姆走去卫星停车场，夕阳西下的时候。

1187
00:58:43.430 --> 00:58:45.590
You guys both look like angels.
你们俩看起来都像天使一样。

1188
00:58:45.990 --> 00:58:48.330
You both look so flippin' adorable.
你们俩看起来真是可爱极了。

1189
00:58:48.770 --> 00:58:51.790
Well, I remember we had to wait in our trailer for that light.
我记得我们为了等那束光在房车里等了很久。

1190
00:58:51.950 --> 00:58:53.750
That's called the magic hour.
那叫“魔幻时刻”。

1191
00:58:53.950 --> 00:58:54.350
Yeah.
没错。

1192
00:58:54.350 --> 00:58:59.610
In the biz, and there's this little 45 minutes when the sun is truly magical.
在业内，那是有着短短45分钟，太阳光线真正神奇的时候。

1193
00:59:00.270 --> 00:59:02.610
Everybody, take your photos at magic hour.
大家，一定要在魔幻时刻拍照。

1194
00:59:02.890 --> 00:59:03.930
It's when you look the beSt.
那是你看起来最棒的时候。

1195
00:59:04.110 --> 00:59:04.550
That's right.
没错。

1196
00:59:04.670 --> 00:59:07.970
If you're planning a wedding, plan for some, like, magic hour photos.
如果你正在筹划婚礼，一定要安排一些魔幻时刻的照片。

1197
00:59:08.450 --> 00:59:08.670
Yeah.
没错。

1198
00:59:08.970 --> 00:59:14.850
So, we waited for that moment, and we could only do a few takes because then we were going to lose the light.
所以，我们一直在等那个瞬间，而且我们只能拍几次，因为之后光线就会消失了。

1199
00:59:15.150 --> 00:59:16.850
He drops to one knee.
他单膝跪下了。

1200
00:59:17.250 --> 00:59:17.690
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1201
00:59:18.170 --> 00:59:23.470
Well, I'll tell you, this moment was promo'd like crazy.
我跟你说，这一刻的宣传力度简直疯狂。

1202
00:59:23.470 --> 00:59:24.170
Crazy.
疯狂。

1203
00:59:24.170 --> 00:59:24.970
Like, crazy.
简直疯狂。

1204
00:59:25.290 --> 00:59:26.950
I bet they blasted it out.
我敢说他们肯定是大肆宣传了一番。

1205
00:59:27.250 --> 00:59:27.730
Yeah.
没错。

1206
00:59:28.050 --> 00:59:33.050
Well, you know, we talked about how season four was interrupted by the writer's strike.
你知道，我们之前聊过第四季是怎么被编剧罢工打断的。

1207
00:59:33.690 --> 00:59:42.910
The writers originally had this very, very big storyline for Jim and Pam that I think involved them moving in together, if I'm correct.
编剧们原本为吉姆和帕姆构思了一个非常非常宏大的故事线，如果我没记错的话，内容涉及他们搬到一起住。

1208
00:59:43.730 --> 00:59:49.190
And instead, because we lost a bunch of episodes, they were like, you know what?
但后来因为我们少拍了好几集，他们就想，要不这样吧？

1209
00:59:49.190 --> 00:59:51.950
We should skip that, and they should just get engaged.
我们跳过那段，直接让他们订婚好了。

1210
00:59:52.130 --> 00:59:56.770
Or we should just skip to the part where we're thinking they might get engaged any minute.
或者直接跳到那种让人觉得他们随时可能订婚的阶段。

1211
00:59:56.770 --> 01:00:00.650
And so, that was where this part of the story came from.
所以，这部分剧情就是这么来的。

1212
01:00:01.330 --> 01:00:01.910
I like it.
我喜欢这个安排。

1213
01:00:02.070 --> 01:00:04.050
I like that Pam still had her own place.
我喜欢帕姆当时还有自己的住处。

1214
01:00:04.350 --> 01:00:04.710
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

1215
01:00:04.790 --> 01:00:10.650
I like all of that storyline for her because you sort of feel like Pam lived with Roy for a long time.
我很喜欢她那条故事线，因为你会觉得帕姆之前和罗伊住在一起很久了。

1216
01:00:11.030 --> 01:00:16.970
And then she finally carved out her own space in the world, and I really liked that choice.
然后她终于在这个世界上开辟出了属于自己的空间，我真的很喜欢这个选择。

1217
01:00:17.270 --> 01:00:21.210
Well, your reaction when you realize that Jim is faking is so great.
当你意识到吉姆是在演戏时，你的反应真是太棒了。

1218
01:00:21.210 --> 01:00:22.170
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

1219
01:00:22.330 --> 01:00:23.210
You're like, I hate you.
你当时就像是说，我讨厌你。

1220
01:00:23.370 --> 01:00:24.310
And he's like, what?
而他却说，怎么了？

1221
01:00:24.330 --> 01:00:25.590
It's really cute.
真的很可爱。

1222
01:00:26.110 --> 01:00:26.390
Yeah.
是啊。

1223
01:00:26.610 --> 01:00:28.470
I have some bad news.
我有坏消息要告诉你。

1224
01:00:28.890 --> 01:00:29.410
What?
什么？

1225
01:00:29.730 --> 01:00:33.010
I mean, spoiler alert, Pam's going to need to go to art school.
我是说，剧透预警，帕姆得去上艺术学校了。

1226
01:00:33.390 --> 01:00:34.950
We're going to frustrate you.
我们要让你感到沮丧了。

1227
01:00:35.110 --> 01:00:35.770
I know.
我知道。

1228
01:00:36.030 --> 01:00:39.630
This proposal's going to take a little while, but we're planting the seeds.
这次求婚还要等上一阵子，但我们正在埋下伏笔。

1229
01:00:39.910 --> 01:00:42.750
They have to pull you guys apart to put you back together.
他们必须先把你们分开，才能让你们重归于好。

1230
01:00:42.930 --> 01:00:43.850
It makes me crazy.
这让我抓狂。

1231
01:00:44.290 --> 01:00:45.210
I know.
我知道。

1232
01:00:45.710 --> 01:00:48.670
Well, guys, that is chair model.
好了，各位，这就是《椅子模特》这一集。

1233
01:00:48.670 --> 01:00:51.050
Well, next up is Night Out.
接下来是《夜出》那一集。

1234
01:00:51.730 --> 01:00:55.150
I'm really enjoying season four, Angela, I have to say.
安吉拉，我不得不说，我真的很享受第四季。

1235
01:00:55.550 --> 01:00:56.310
Me too.
我也是。

1236
01:00:56.690 --> 01:00:57.790
So fun.
太有趣了。

1237
01:00:57.990 --> 01:01:02.490
And for all of you chair models out there, just know your work is not in vain.
对于所有像椅子模特一样的人，要知道你们的努力没有白费。

1238
01:01:02.690 --> 01:01:06.030
You might be inspiring others to find true love.
你们可能正在激励他人去寻找真爱。

1239
01:01:06.410 --> 01:01:13.710
And Paul, thank you so much for sending in these audio clips and being so quick to respond
还有保罗，非常感谢你发来这些音频片段，并且在我发短信时回复得那么快。

1240
01:01:13.710 --> 01:01:14.690
when I texted you.
你真是太令人愉快了，我非常喜欢你。

1241
01:01:14.850 --> 01:01:18.070
You are just such a delight, and I adore you.
你真是太令人愉快了，我非常喜欢你。

1242
01:01:18.070 --> 01:01:19.710
And these made our day, Jenna.
这些让我们今天过得很开心，珍娜。

1243
01:01:19.950 --> 01:01:22.890
And you guys, 1-800-PREPARE.com.
还有各位，请访问 1-800-PREPARE.com。

1244
